## Defect under test

The catch-up loop in src/shared/missed-sweep.ts records a cycle as missed when its
DATE is before `today`, while the open occurrence correctly uses the supersede rule
(`today >= next(open)`). For non-daily rules this marks the still-running cycle as
missed. D-A: a cycle is missed only when `today` reaches the NEXT occurrence's date.

## armReminders reading

`armReminders = successor.date >= today` (phase 1 contract, unchanged). The corrected
successor is the cycle still running at `today`; when its date is before `today`
(monthly 12-05 vs today 12-10; weekly 10-12 vs today 10-14) it is an open occurrence
dated in the past, so `armReminders: false` (PRD D-B / AC-4: past-dated open
successor without Reminders). It stays completable late; only its Reminders are not armed.

